# expiry2 — SET ... EX, and why SET wipes a TTL
#
# Learn: a plain SET replaces the value AND removes any TTL the key had.
# So "EXPIRE, then SET" silently produces a key that never expires. The
# fix is to set value and TTL together: SET key value EX seconds (or PX
# for milliseconds). One command, atomic, no window without a TTL.
#
# Task: cache the forecast "sunny, 21C" under cache:weather:paris for
# 60 seconds.
#

EXPIRE cache:weather:paris 60
SET cache:weather:paris "sunny, 21C"
